{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_125e6c956836aeae5d6945b60ac9b51680ce49f13f182fa4b78058e7adcbf20f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_99fe04a7266dab677a3600680c08225dca4f22b57d1457618e99238ffe7d9acb"],"source_ids":["src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"The product has two layers: Smithy (@stoneforge/smithy), the installable orchestrator that spawns agents and manages sessions and worktree isolation, and Quarry (@stoneforge/quarry), an event-sourced data SDK usable standalone.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1fea9e832046b980b7ecf0b2dc11b657626b7bc9d41f00914d2e4969bff2ed00","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_004733a362e50c62517615e866b8617676370bd6b76c041d3cadd11428f94b29","slc_f03d7d3b5c1d92d34e167740a00e93bffff079b1fdcde93ae9e38134ce8b6f41"],"source_ids":["src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"The orchestration loop: a Director plans tasks with priorities and dependencies, a dispatch daemon assigns ready tasks to idle workers, workers execute in isolated git worktrees, and a merge steward runs tests and squash-merges or hands off on failure.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_224d3d55407bf5fc0c65faf1b780c3052e184494adc9ed038876eeead23dde96","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6d2d3422e61bd5dea5e770cbda460c04f1c0483cab63989620c6fe7eb399a56e","slc_82b6532600b6f7baded959ab2a13f9a178f391be983b04c818aa997b954a652f","slc_a5ca2e1936c769a4fbdb2ae85c78eccd506c0807cf6c6dbc8ea34aef87cee19b","slc_d36e37c8d69c20dcbad357e8fe8784acd0d03a148a77b74d3a1539377263a92a"],"source_ids":["src_4b94fc2734c45bbd895d873212f34012","src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors use pnpm/bun commands (pnpm install, pnpm build, pnpm test, pnpm lint, pnpm typecheck; bun test), tests are colocated as *.test.ts files, and contributors must sign a CLA before PR merge.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_23bb1ff9568a05d3c83aed532a32eb42daebd231da28e9a5116aa979e439365e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_563d457bbe8581cbb7d6fafaba7491877f682ce8539f2d53f65f0b0a5a0ccef1"],"source_ids":["src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"Agents run autonomously with permissions bypassed and no human approval gates before actions, an intentional design the README says means agents read, write, execute, and push code without asking.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_281e75c677be867fea42ae3a06df879445c059e55c95c4ecb1acf166bc175f27","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_02a57f8735023560fdfb17441c060067d7b5eb8428d824ed7329e1307d92552f","slc_468cc962d3a3037d396620328f594a52989e8ca66c250fa3915e3456a76da9e8"],"source_ids":["src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"The monorepo ships packages core, storage, quarry, smithy, ui, and shared-routes, plus apps quarry-server (port 3456), quarry-web (5173), smithy-server (3457), and smithy-web (5174).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_39bea180497cf7073bc8827e3689cd8bdf12a1874fcecad99635f7f520ebc521","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_304a8e1d1eed7e87a01cef28d7cd878d794730510792e81fd27e927faafd2702","slc_c5c46d95b140c4adf5e0c2a100c3f517b34acce17479f0846aec58230772ac50"],"source_ids":["src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"Built-in role prompts can be overridden per project via .stoneforge/prompts/ files such as director.md, worker.md, and steward-merge.md.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7c359d0fb0a3cda1145b8a5bb26913d4ec3ed9c7b05f26b572c837b0fd36f30d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bdb138e6e22fb2cd4f4eb7d674846d2bc796b6e9a41d8a39b1aa790133639f60","slc_ebfbad966fd16e541f3a9dcd68305e90e4db72e5873b59a98213173a76b46dcc","slc_f174b22a6813cf32814202d04a12204670d5813f2ab4d3df4888f70008fbd000"],"source_ids":["src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"Agent roles include Director (persistent planner), ephemeral workers spawned by the daemon, persistent workers started manually, and stewards for merge review, docs, recovery, and custom workflows; the dispatch daemon is a background process started with 'sf daemon start'.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7c56c7cf7b30f6e6c8c4677e548db929e732a690a8cee8139cde65cfd2001b01","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4d66e430c32ea5385d3473fde5d20bb4d0d75e6b6f40bc43b967bfd0ee89a748","slc_c944e90856d1937776d58683a7c1d0af306c519e1918559b0703f5a3a205b9fb"],"source_ids":["src_4b94fc2734c45bbd895d873212f34012"],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md instructs contributing agents that 'blocked' status is computed from dependencies and must never be set directly, and that api.addDependency() does not detect cycles, so DependencyService.detectCycle() should be used.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b678268bb6752e6f5e8045026ce3c21efa6fd8b13f5ca6275bce2261a614c11f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"stoneforge-ai/stoneforge@0a7052a9ffa1 snapshot ad29787df384c1d7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5c49e2bd457be6034eb0d9d9d6f342b8ea57c436580a7336a0345a62035d19c6","slc_a55fc85d8f62400bd7460418ef40b37a8faf7df73d04315f39df60eea3c6e6ee"],"source_ids":["src_4ee8cc5628b157a682b6ca9e26d76140"],"text":"Storage uses a dual model: SQLite serves as an ephemeral cache with FTS5 full-text search and indexes, while git-tracked append-only JSONL is the durable source of truth, rebuilt into SQLite on sync.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:43:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e4f575487d1742228087641f1cae202c"}
